|* Post-layout ro_array_core (whole array, real inter-ring wiring) with the
|* shared substrate node left FLOATING -- the array-scale sibling of
|* sim/post-layout-ro-ring5/testbench/tb_post_layout_substrate_float.spice,
|* now over the REAL composed array GDS (real physical ring-to-ring
|* proximity, well spacing and shared psub geometry, not four separately
|* extracted leaf cells hand-tied to a shared node as if placed at infinite
|* separation -- see DR-0005's own "Proximity" limitation, which this deck
|* closes for the substrate mechanism specifically).
|*
|* Purpose (DR-0003 section 8's inter-ring decorrelation gap; DR-0005's own
|* "Follow-up required" section: "Findings 1 and 3 should be re-run against
|* the assembled block when it exists"). This deck differs from
|* tb_post_layout_ro_array_core.spice's post-layout half in exactly one
|* respect: that deck ties `vsubs` hard to 0 (`Vsub vsubs 0 dc 0`), this one
|* does not tie it at all, leaving it on
|* layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice's own
|* `Rvsubs_dctie vsubs 0 1e+12` (klayout-tools#1503). The pair brackets the
|* real answer the same way DR-0005's ring-level pair did:
|*
|*   TIED   (sibling deck, already run) -- ideal zero-impedance substrate,
|*          no inter-ring coupling possible by construction.
|*   FLOAT  (this deck) -- ideal infinite-impedance shared substrate: every
|*          ring's switching current is forced through the shared node's
|*          capacitance and into every other ring.
|*
|* No pre-layout control: a pre-layout netlist has no substrate node, so it
|* has nothing to say about this question (same choice
|* tb_post_layout_substrate_float.spice made at ring scope).
|*
|* Measured: each ring's own period (line for line comparable against the
|* sibling tied deck's p_tr1-p_tr4 at the same corner/temp/vdd), the array
|* skew span, and the substrate node's own peak-to-peak excursion -- the
|* direct measure of how hard the four rings (now WITH the buffer + XOR tree
|* load, both riding the same block vdd, also present) are driving each
|* other through it.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* ff, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice, 125.0 and 1.98. As committed it is not a
|* runnable deck. Invoke with
|* `--pex-lib layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice` (no --ro-ring5
|* needed: this deck includes only the post-layout library).
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" ff
|
|* post-layout ARRAY subcircuit library only -- no pre-layout control, see
|* header for why.
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex-array/ro_array_core_pex.spice"
|
|.temp 125.0
|
|* --- substrate return node: FLOATING (see header) -- no Vsub source ----
|
|Vddrp1 pvddr1 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp2 pvddr2 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp3 pvddr3 0 dc 1.98
|Vddrp4 pvddr4 0 dc 1.98
|Vddp pvdd 0 dc 1.98
|Venp1 pen1 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp2 pen2 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp3 pen3 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|Venp4 pen4 0 PULSE(0 1.98 5n 100p 100p 1u 2u)
|xarr pen1 pen2 pen3 pen4 pvddr1 pvddr2 pvddr3 pvddr4 pvdd 0 pxo pro1 pro2 pro3 pro4 ro_array_core_pex
|
|.ic v(pro1)=0
|.ic v(pro2)=0
|.ic v(pro3)=0
|.ic v(pro4)=0
|
|.save v(pro1) v(pro2) v(pro3) v(pro4) v(xarr.vsubs)
|.save i(Vddrp1) i(Vddrp2) i(Vddrp3) i(Vddrp4) i(Vddp)
|
|.tran 5p 800n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|meas tran pt1a when v(pro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt1b when v(pro1)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr1 = (pt1b - pt1a)/10
|meas tran pt2a when v(pro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt2b when v(pro2)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr2 = (pt2b - pt2a)/10
|meas tran pt3a when v(pro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt3b when v(pro3)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr3 = (pt3b - pt3a)/10
|meas tran pt4a when v(pro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran pt4b when v(pro4)=0.5*1.98 rise=13
|let p_tr4 = (pt4b - pt4a)/10
|let p_skew_span = p_tr1/p_tr4
|
|meas tran vsub_max MAX v(xarr.vsubs) from=100n to=800n
|meas tran vsub_min MIN v(xarr.vsubs) from=100n to=800n
|let vsub_swing_frac = (vsub_max - vsub_min) / 1.98
|
|print p_tr1
|print p_tr2
|print p_tr3
|print p_tr4
|print p_skew_span
|print vsub_swing_frac
|.endc
|.end
|

